From ecfae110f4257e50ec6c53c38ed75f8056eac65b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 08:03:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(track): /api/track for treegens.app/track, tree tracking
 with no crypto

A public route for the planting capture with the crypto taken out: a
phone films a tree's land and plant clips through the same resumable
upload sessions as a planting, and they are stored as TrackClip rows,
never as Submissions. Nothing here touches users, verifiers, rewards,
OTC or MGRO.

- TrackClip model: one row per clip; the land clip's _id is the tree id.
- trackService: store a clip, link a plant to its land (same phone only),
  dashboard list and totals, CSV manifest, URL list, admin delete.
- routes/track.ts: upload sessions behind an x-track-device phone id
  (buildUploadSessionRouter), GET /trees, /trees/:id, /totals,
  /trees.csv, /urls.txt, /config, DELETE /trees/:id (TRACK_ADMIN_KEY).
- uploadSessionService: a session made on the track route gets channel
  'track' and is stored by trackService; it never guesses a land by
  filming time.
- gwrAiCountService: the sweeps take a target collection. GWR behaves as
  before; /track counts mangrove plant clips only, like plantings.
- Tests: 13 route tests through the real session protocol, including the
  AI sweep over track clips. Full suite passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
